For whoever's on the PC or SPC of @AcmSIGecom #AcmEC25 and is struggling with keeping track of their bids, here's a small script, courtesy of GPT-4o, that if run in the Chroms console, will count for you how many papers you have rated at each bid level so far. Happy bidding! :)
var inputs = document.querySelectorAll('input.revpref');
var frequencyMap = {};
inputs.forEach(function(input) {
var value = input.value;
if (frequencyMap[value] !== undefined) {
frequencyMap[value]++;
} else {
frequencyMap[value] = 1;
}
});
function generateHistogram(frequencyMap) {
var histogramString = '';
for (var value in frequencyMap) {
if (frequencyMap.hasOwnProperty(value)) {
histogramString += `${value}: ` + `${frequencyMap[value]}\n`;
}
}
return histogramString;
}
console.log("Bid Summary:");
console.log(generateHistogram(frequencyMap));

@boazbaraktcs An interesting interaction between STOC's new arxiv policy and arXiv's new one-strike policy is that if you violate the one-strike policy, you seem to get a lifetime ban from STOC. Not necessary unreasonable but I wonder if intentional.
Quoting @tdietterich
The penalty is a 1-year ban from arXiv followed by the requirement that subsequent arXiv submissions must first be accepted at a reputable peer-reviewed venue. 4/
